    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe only test class is `AcceptanceTest` (the others are support/base classes); the full suite passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, **BUILD SUCCESS**).\n\n### Change made\n\nI updated `generateCustomerCode` in `ClinicServiceImpl.java` to produce the new `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` format:\n\n- **CITY3** \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the owner's `city`\n- **LAST3** \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the `lastName`\n- **NNNN** \u2014 a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence, computed as one more than the number of owners already in that city (new helper `countOwnersInCity`, matching city case-insensitively \u2014 consistent with the existing `countNamesakes` style)\n\nThe call site now passes both `owner.getCity()` and `owner.getLastName()`.\n\n### Derived values rebuilt automatically\n\n`membershipNumber` in `OwnerMapper` is formatted as `'<customerCode>-M<YY>'` directly from `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so it now naturally reflects the new format (e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26`) with no further change needed. No other code derives values from `customerCode`.\n\nThe acceptance test's regex `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}` is satisfied by the new output (e.g. `LON-SMI-0001`).\n\nNote: this repo isn't a git repository, so there's nothing to commit.",
