        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is coherent, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase.\n\n- The new `countOwnersInCity` helper is placed right next to the existing `countNamesakes` helper and mirrors its exact shape (null guard \u2192 `ownerRepository.findAll().stream().filter(...).count()`), so a maintainer here would find it immediately natural. Extracting it rather than inlining the stream into `generateCustomerCode` keeps that method focused on formatting.\n- `generateCustomerCode` grows the `city` parameter and a parallel `city3`/`last3` derivation; the logic stays in the same unit it was already in, and the Javadoc was updated to match the new format.\n- The \"membership number\" the spec mentions is derived in `OwnerMapper.formatMembershipNumber` from `owner.getCustomerCode()` (`\"%s-M%02d\"`). Because it composes on top of the stored customer code rather than re-deriving the format, it rebuilds on the new format automatically \u2014 correctly, no duplicated format logic was introduced there, and nothing in that unit needed to change for structure's sake.\n\nNo duplication, no catch-all accretion, logic sits where the rest of the owner-derivation helpers live."
